# SPA routing for the app.
#
# THE RULES BELOW THIS HEADER ARE GENERATED. Do not add them by hand -- they are
# derived from App.tsx by app/scripts/assemble.ts, so a route and its rule can
# never disagree. Add a <Route> and the rule appears on the next build.
#
# Why not a single catch-all, which is what every SPA guide suggests:
#
#   /app/*  /app/index.html  200
#     Silently discarded. Pages canonicalises /app/index.html back to /app/,
#     re-matching the pattern, so it detects an infinite loop and drops the rule.
#     wrangler warns about it; the deployed site says nothing and serves the
#     landing page for every route inside the app.
#
#   /app/*  /app-shell  200
#     Parses cleanly and is far worse. Cloudflare evaluates _redirects BEFORE
#     static files -- the reverse of Netlify -- so a catch-all rewrites every
#     script, the stylesheet, the manifest and the service worker to HTML, and
#     the app never boots.
#
# The generator refuses to emit /app/*, and refuses any prefix that would shadow
# /app/assets, /app/icons, /app/screenshots or /app/video. CI rejects a
# catch-all too, in case anyone edits this file directly.
